  "sidebar": {
    "logoText": "VECT-AI workshops and exhibit documentation ",
    "items": [
      {
        "id": "info-icon",
        "label": "About Project",
        "content": "<p><em>Cracks of Meaning</em> is a 3D documentation of a pilot workshop on critical thinking about AI through videopoetry in art education. The workshop was carried out by the VECT-AI collective within the CAPHE project, and its original presentation took place at The Design Pharmacy (Apteka Designu) in Kraków, 12–15 March 2026.</p><p>The public outcome of the process was the immersive videopoem <em>Obowiązki własnej ręki wciągniętej ( ) do środka (Duties of One’s Own Hand Drawn ( ) Inward)</em> — a nonlinear composition of text, image and sound, developed through work with error, deformation and ambiguity.</p><p>This virtual archive consists of two rooms. The first room documents the workshop process and presents the accompanying workshop manual. The second room is dedicated to multimedia documentation of the final outcome of the two-day workshop: <em>Obowiązki własnej ręki wciągniętej ( ) do środka</em>. The work was created collaboratively by workshop participants, leaders and the curatorial team: Wojciech Brzozowski, Justyna Gorzkowicz, Kamila Koziołek, Aleksandra Łukaszewicz, Jarosław Solecki, Mikołaj Straus, Joanna Szczepanik, Lilly Venyan and Beata Winiarska.</p><p>The virtual exhibition space was created from a 3D scan of the original venue. A detailed discussion of the workshop method, structure and project assumptions is available in the accompanying documentation.</p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "vectai-zenodo",
        "label": "Zenodo: Cracks of Meaning",
        "link": "https://zenodo.org/records/19220100"
      },
      {
        "id": "bpa-home",
        "label": "Blue Point Art homepage",
        "link": "https://bluepointart.uk/cracks-of-meaning-in-the-bpaa/"
      }
    ]
  },
